# MC-X-F12 (writer 9). L §4.3: "A fact is law-dated when its value can change with the law date: an input, band, def or rule with a row or version whose span isn't `always`". rate's two rows sit in v_act, which governs always, so rate isn't
# law-dated, and r, which reads it and age3 (governs always), reads nothing law-dated: rule 2, it needs no at.
# rate(3) = 400.00 PLN ("under 6"). snap12: LOAD-LAWDATE r reads law-dated facts and states no at.
=== m.tally
model f12
  tally 2
  on 2027-12-31
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
  note "MC-X-F12: a band whose every row governs always is read by a def that states no at (L 4.3: not law-dated)."

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

source act "the act"


input age3: int

band rate(a: int): money PLN

def r[m in months]: money PLN = rate(age3)

ask q: r[2027-05]

version v_act
  cite act
  governs always
  known 2026-12-01
  age3 = 3 "the age"
  rate: [0, 6) = 400.00 PLN "under 6"
  rate: [6, 18) = 250.00 PLN "6 to 17"
=== expect
q: 400.00 PLN
  cut 2027-12-31
